    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1237">

                <pb facs="1131" n="873" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg873"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/1892</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Spring
                        Rice</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I beg to acknowledge
                    your informal letter of the 27th instant, in which you bring to my attention
                    certain information in your possession relative to the operations of British
                    warships in the Pacific and in particular the report that the British steamship
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Bellerophon</hi> coaled His Majesty’s ship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Rainbow</hi> on the 27th of February within a mile of
                    Anacapa Island.</p>
                <p>I am bringing this matter at once to the attention of my Government and shall
                    take pleasure in communicating further with you upon the subject as soon as I am
                    in a position to do so.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cecil Spring Rice</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
